          "title": "You'll want to know: امانت",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "امانت — amānat — \"something left in one's keeping\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "اگر اس نے امانت لوٹائی تو میں خوش ہوں گا۔ agar us ne amānat lauṭāī to maiṅ khush hūṅ gā. If he gives back what I left with him, I will be glad."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Feminine."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "امانت (amānat) is usually traced, through Persian, to Arabic amāna, \"trustworthiness; a thing entrusted\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
